}

{
  "decision": "covered",
  "policy_quotes": [
    "Effective for services performed on or after March 15, 2005, when recognized clinical risk factors are employed to select patients for transplantation, high dose melphalan (HDM) together with AuSCT is reasonable and necessary for Medicare beneficiaries of any age group with primary amyloid light chain (AL) amyloidosis who meet the following criteria: - Amyloid deposition in 2 or fewer organs; and, - Cardiac left ventricular ejection fraction (EF) greater than 45%."
  ],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient meets all coverage criteria for autologous stem cell transplantation with high-dose melphalan for primary AL amyloidosis. He has amyloid deposition in exactly two organs (kidneys and heart), his left ventricular ejection fraction of 55% exceeds the required 45% threshold, and the team employed recognized clinical risk factors for patient selection as specified in the policy. No additional documentation appears to be missing for this covered indication."
}

{
  "decision": "not_covered",
  "policy_quotes": ["Effective for services performed on or after March 15, 2005, when recognized clinical risk factors are employed to select patients for transplantation, high dose melphalan (HDM) together with AuSCT is reasonable and necessary for Medicare beneficiaries of any age group with primary amyloid light chain (AL) amyloidosis who meet the following criteria: - Cardiac left ventricular ejection fraction (EF) greater than 45%."],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient has primary AL amyloidosis with involvement limited to two organs (kidneys and heart), meeting the first criterion. However, the documented left ventricular ejection fraction is exactly 45%, which does not satisfy the requirement for an EF greater than 45%. Since this criterion is not met, the service is not covered under the NCD."
}

{
  "decision": "not_covered",
  "policy_quotes": [
    "Tandem transplantation (multiple rounds of AuSCT) for patients with multiple myeloma;",
    "In these cases, AuSCT is not considered reasonable and necessary within the meaning of §l862(a)(1)(A) of the Act and is not covered under Medicare."
  ],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The policy explicitly lists tandem transplantation (multiple rounds of AuSCT) for multiple myeloma as a nationally non-covered indication. The patient has Durie-Salmon Stage III multiple myeloma and is requesting a second autologous transplant as part of a planned tandem protocol, which falls directly under this exclusion. No exceptions or coverage criteria exist for this scenario under the current NCD."
}

{
  "decision": "covered",
  "policy_quotes": [
    "Effective October 1, 2000, single AuSCT is only covered for Durie-Salmon Stage II or III patients that fit the following requirements: - Newly diagnosed or responsive multiple myeloma. This includes those patients with at least a partial response to prior chemotherapy (defined as a 50% decrease either in measurable paraprotein [serum and/or urine] or in bone marrow infiltration, sustained for at least 1 month), and those in responsive relapse; and - Adequate cardiac, renal, pulmonary, and hepatic function."
  ],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient meets all coverage criteria for autologous stem cell transplantation for multiple myeloma. She has Durie-Salmon Stage III disease, achieved a partial response (55% decrease in serum M-protein sustained for 6 weeks), and demonstrates adequate organ function with LVEF 60%, creatinine clearance 65 mL/min, DLCO 78%, and normal liver tests. Since this is a single autologous transplant request for a patient without prior transplantation, it falls within the nationally covered indications."
}

{
  "decision": "not_covered",
  "policy_quotes": ["Autologous Stem Cell Transplantation (AuSCT) is considered reasonable and necessary under §1862(a)(1)(A) of the Act for the following conditions and is covered under Medicare for patients with: Acute leukemia in remission who have a high probability of relapse and who have no human leucocyte antigens (HLA)-matched", "Insufficient data exist to establish definite conclusions regarding the efficacy of AuSCT for the following conditions: Acute leukemia not in remission"],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient has acute myeloid leukemia that is primary refractory (not in remission), as evidenced by 30% blasts after induction therapy. The policy explicitly states AuSCT is covered only for acute leukemia in remission with no HLA-matched donor, and is non-covered for acute leukemia not in remission. Since the leukemia is not in remission, the service does not meet the coverage criteria."
}

{
  "decision": "insufficient_documentation",
  "policy_quotes": ["Effective October 1, 2000, single AuSCT is only covered for Durie-Salmon Stage II or III patients that fit the following requirements: - Adequate cardiac, renal, pulmonary, and hepatic function."],
  "missing_documentation": ["Echocardiogram results", "Pulmonary function testing results", "Renal function results", "Hepatic function results", "Statement about organ function adequacy"],
  "rationale": "The patient meets the initial criteria for AuSCT coverage with Durie-Salmon Stage II multiple myeloma and sustained partial response to prior chemotherapy. However, the policy explicitly requires documentation of adequate cardiac, renal, pulmonary, and hepatic function for coverage. The submitted record lacks all required organ function testing results and assessments, making it impossible to verify compliance with this mandatory criterion."
}

{
  "decision": "not_covered",
  "policy_quotes": [
    "Insufficient data exist to establish definite conclusions regarding the efficacy of AuSCT for the following conditions: - Solid tumors (other than neuroblastoma)",
    "In these cases, AuSCT is not considered reasonable and necessary within the meaning of §l862(a)(1)(A) of the Act and is not covered under Medicare."
  ],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient has a metastatic nonseminomatous germ cell tumor, which is classified as a solid tumor other than neuroblastoma. The NCD explicitly states that autologous stem cell transplantation is not covered for solid tumors other than neuroblastoma due to insufficient evidence of efficacy. Since the requested service is AuSCT for a non-covered indication, it does not meet Medicare coverage criteria."
}

{
  "decision": "not_covered",
  "policy_quotes": ["Palliative treatment of skin manifestations of cutaneous T-cell lymphoma that has not responded to other therapy."],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient has Sézary syndrome (a form of cutaneous T-cell lymphoma) but has received no prior therapy, while the NCD explicitly requires that the skin manifestations have 'not responded to other therapy' for coverage. Since this is the first treatment requested, the criterion for prior treatment failure is not met. All other indications remain non-covered under section C of the policy."
}

{
  "decision": "covered",
  "policy_quotes": [
    "Effective December 19, 2006, Medicare also provides coverage for: Patients with acute cardiac allograft rejection whose disease is refractory to standard immunosuppressive drug treatment"
  ],
  "missing_documentation": [],
  "rationale": "The patient meets all coverage criteria for extracorporeal photopheresis under NCD 110.4. He has acute cardiac allograft rejection (grade 2R endomyocardial biopsy) that is refractory to standard immunosuppressive treatment, having failed both pulse steroids and antithymocyte globulin. The documentation clearly shows the rejection persists despite these standard therapies, satisfying the requirement for refractory disease."
}

{
